<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">About this report</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    This report is an evidence digest. It summarises findings published by researchers and institutions in 2025 and 2026 on three questions: does AI tutoring improve learning, does AI reduce teacher workload, and who is actually using these tools. Zunkiree Labs did not conduct any of the surveys or trials. We read the published sources, extracted the figures, and added notes on what each can and cannot support.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Where we offer a view of our own, it is marked as ours. A fuller narrative is in our ebook, <a href="/resources/ai-in-education-evidence-ebook/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">AI in Education: What the Trials and Surveys Show</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Key findings</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <li><strong>Tutor design decides the outcome.</strong> A Harvard randomized crossover trial (194 students analysed) found a carefully designed AI tutor produced higher post-test scores than an active-learning lesson, with a median 4.5 against 3.5. A PNAS field experiment with nearly 1,000 students found students who practised with a standard chatbot interface scored 17% lower on a later exam without it than students who never had access.</li>
    <li><strong>Practice performance can mislead.</strong> The OECD reports that AI access improved short-term performance in the Turkish experiment by 48% with the standard interface and 127% with a tutoring version, yet students performed 17% worse once access was removed.</li>
    <li><strong>Teachers report real time savings.</strong> Weekly AI users in a Gallup survey of 2,232 US public school teachers estimate saving 5.9 hours a week. The figure is self-reported and applies to the 32% who use AI at least weekly.</li>
    <li><strong>Use is uneven.</strong> About half of US adults use AI chatbots according to Pew, while Microsoft estimates 18.8% of people aged 15 to 64 worldwide used a generative AI product in Q2 2026, with 28.8% in the Global North and 16.2% in the Global South.</li>
    <li><strong>Integrity is a live concern.</strong> The OECD reports that seven in ten teachers on average believe AI could let students present others’ work as their own.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Finding 1. AI tutoring: promising under specific conditions</h2>
  <div class="mb-5 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full min-w-[640px] text-left"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Source</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Design</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Reported result</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Main limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12179260/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kestin et al., Scientific Reports, 2025</a></td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Randomized crossover; 194 analysed of 233 enrolled; two topics, two weeks</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Median post-test 4.5 vs 3.5; estimated effect about 0.63 standard deviations; median time with tutor 49 minutes; engagement rated 4.1 vs 3.6 on a five-point scale</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">One course, short topics, high-achieving students, expert-written prompts</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><a href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/nas/journl/v122y2025pe2422633122.html" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bastani et al., PNAS, 2025</a></td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Field experiment, nearly 1,000 high school math students</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">17% lower grades after removal of unguarded access; guardrailed tutor largely mitigated the harm</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Short period; one subject and country</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><a href="https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/education/From-chalkboards-to-chatbots-Transforming-learning-in-Nigeria" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">World Bank, January 2025</a></td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Six-week after-school pilot, Benin City, Nigeria, with teacher support</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">About 0.3 standard deviations of learning gain reported by the authors</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Authors’ own summary; no sample sizes given; not peer-reviewed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    The Harvard authors state that they do not presume structured AI tutoring will always beat in-class active learning, for example where complex synthesis and higher-order critical thinking are needed. They list conditions that may matter, including a heterogeneous class, a capable model, expert-written prompts and a carefully structured framework.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Finding 2. Teacher workload: savings reported, student impact unmeasured</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    The <a href="https://news.gallup.com/poll/691967/three-teachers-weekly-saving-six-weeks-year.aspx" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gallup report</a> (June 24, 2025) surveyed 2,232 US public K-12 teachers between March 18 and April 11, 2025, using the RAND American Teacher Panel. Gallup reports a margin of error of plus or minus 2.5 percentage points.
  </p>
  <div class="mb-5 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-left"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Measure</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Reported figure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Teachers who used AI for work</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">60% (32% weekly or more, 28% monthly or less)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Estimated weekly time saved, weekly users</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">5.9 hours, about six weeks over a 37.4-week school year</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Top uses (monthly or more)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Preparing to teach 37%, worksheets and activities 33%, modifying materials 28%</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Teachers saying quality improved at least somewhat</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">57% (grading and feedback) to 74% (administrative work)</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Teachers saying quality got worse</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Fewer than 16%</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    The <a href="https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/oecd-digital-education-outlook-2026_062a7394-en.html" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OECD</a> adds that in its 2024 TALIS survey 37% of teachers used generative AI for work tasks, and it cites a 31% reduction in lesson and resource planning time for secondary science teachers in England and a 9 percentage-point increase in student pass rates when low-experience tutors used AI support.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    None of these figures show that students learned more.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Finding 3. Adoption: widely used, unevenly spread</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/06/PI_2026.06.17_Americans-and-AI_REPORT.pdf" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pew Research Center</a> surveyed 5,119 US adults in February 2026: about half use AI chatbots, roughly one in four daily, and 38% of employed adults use them for work tasks. <a href="https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2026/09/21/the-continued-state-of-global-ai-diffusion-in-2026/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft</a> estimates 18.8% worldwide, and says the Global North and South gap is widening. The <a href="https://hai.stanford.edu/ai-index/2026-ai-index-report" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stanford 2026 AI Index</a> reports 53% population adoption of generative AI within three years and a strong link between adoption and GDP per capita.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    These numbers use different definitions and populations, so they should not be placed side by side. We found no Nepal-specific figure in them.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">What the evidence cannot tell you</h2>
  <ul class="mb-5 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <li><strong>Whether gains last.</strong> The OECD notes most evidence is short-term; the World Bank team lists long-term effects as unknown.</li>
    <li><strong>Whether results travel.</strong> No cited trial or survey was run in Nepal.</li>
    <li><strong>Whether teacher time savings reach students.</strong> Gallup notes teachers reinvest saved time, but the survey does not test the effect on learning.</li>
    <li><strong>Whether quality ratings are accurate.</strong> They are teachers’ own judgements.</li>
    <li><strong>How privacy and equity play out.</strong> The tutoring trials do not examine student data handling or who lacks access.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    This report should not be read as showing that AI improves learning in general. It shows that some designs helped, some harmed, and that measurement matters.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">What to do with this</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Our own suggestions, not findings from the studies:
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-5 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <li>If you run a school or training program, start with a teacher-facing task and a recorded baseline. Our step-by-step <a href="/resources/introduce-ai-school-training-program-guide/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">guide to introducing AI safely</a> sets out a pilot plan and checklist.</li>
    <li>If you assess an AI tutor, ask whether it gives hints or answers, what it was compared against, and what happens to student performance when it is switched off.</li>
    <li>If you handle student inquiries at an education consultancy, the lower-risk pattern is fast replies on maintained information with a handoff to a counsellor. See our <a href="/resources/ai-student-inquiries-education-consultancies-whitepaper/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">whitepaper on student inquiries</a>.</li>
    <li>Plan for uneven access and skills among students and staff, per the adoption data above.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    To discuss a pilot, <a href="/schedule-a-call/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">schedule a call</a> or read about our <a href="/solutions/custom-agent/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">custom AI agent development</a>.
  </p>
</div>

