<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is this original research?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">No. This is a digest of published studies and surveys. Zunkiree Labs did not run any of the surveys or trials cited, and every figure is attributed to its source in the Sources section.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is the main finding?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">The design of the AI tool decides the outcome. A carefully designed tutor beat an active-learning lesson in one Harvard trial, while unguarded chatbot access led to lower later scores in a PNAS field experiment.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">How much time do teachers say AI saves?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">In a Gallup survey of 2,232 US public school teachers, weekly AI users estimated 5.9 hours saved per week. The 5.9-hour figure applies to the 32% who use AI at least weekly and is self-reported.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do these results apply to Nepal?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Not directly. The trials were run in the United States, Turkey and Nigeria, and the teacher survey covers US teachers. We did not find comparable Nepal-specific studies in these sources, so local pilots are needed.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

